{# The plan-first protocol.

   **Guarded by the todo writers.** A run whose tools hold `read_todo` and none of the
   writers gets an empty text here, so no run is told to call a todo tool it does not have.

   **When it applies is a mechanical rule, not a judgement.** `read_todo` reports
   `needs_plan`, which is true exactly when there is no plan yet or every item is
   resolved. Asking the model instead to decide whether a follow-up question started a new
   investigation is a judgement it makes inconsistently, and the answer would be
   unauditable either way.

   The prose before `write_todo` is part of the answer, and the reasoning disclosure does
   not hide it (`ResearchStreamWriter._keeps_preamble`). A user reads and corrects it there.

   Kept short, because small models read it and follow a long instruction in full.
#}
{% if has('read_todo') and has('write_todo') and has('mark_todo') and has('edit_todo') %}
Before you start work, call {{ tool('read_todo') }}. If it reports `needs_plan`, then in your first
reply, before any other tool call:

1. restate what you understand the task to be, in one or two sentences;
2. give two or three approaches you could take, each with one sentence on its
   trade-off;
3. call {{ tool('write_todo') }} with the approach you chose as the goal, and with `steps`, a list of short sentences.

Then do the work, and call {{ tool('mark_todo') }} as each step is finished or {{ tool('edit_todo') }} when the
plan itself has to change. Keep the list accurate: a step you are abandoning is
`cancelled` with a note saying why, never left pending or quietly deleted.
{% endif %}
